      "dcterms:description": "{\"action\":\"\",\"actor\":\"\",\"alternative_quotes\":[],\"applies_to\":[],\"assertion_ids\":[\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:553d3e17b268e5326b809bb1f20317a77090a8a8f1d21c2507b7158de3751f8f\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:da397e105b9cc7444575fc326b178cf7cac48feae0c7330275691f42d134cc2e\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:0b55ab540e6d53b67b8804b3b503cd3cf77750eb3591544f0823b603e3ff7b8e\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:51856a2677783abe3010543fe6ce15a920a6514a5b52893498ad1bfd0767f709\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:387c27e6bfd93578a2e4689955b7bf427bd76af988941e4b17fb988c33c7429c\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:8c8d3ea7c0a12d12de2905e3bac5b2c71b5a1ac103f0b8d07df7755b071e2f44\"],\"choice_quote\":\"(5) A generator shall mark or label the generator's container with the following:\\n\\n(a) The words \\\"Hazardous Waste\\\"; and\\n\\n(b) An indication of the hazards of the contents [examples include, but are not limited to, the applicable hazardous waste characteristics (i.e., ignitable, corrosive, reactive, toxic); hazard communication consistent with the department of transportation requirements at 49 CFR Part 172 subpart E (labeling) or subpart F (placarding); a hazard statement or pictogram consistent with the occupational safety and health administration hazard communication standard at 29 CFR 1910.1200; or a chemical hazard label consistent with the national fire protection association code 704].\",\"choice_text\":\"both (a) The words \\\"Hazardous Waste\\\" and (b) An indication of the hazards of the contents\",\"claimants\":[],\"concepts\":[],\"context_quotes\":[],\"effective_periods\":[],\"end\":3895,\"evidence\":[{\"end\":3895,\"field\":\"summary\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:3195:3895:sha256-dbc57e737acb25c82f0f782bff280c06f1e03967db4408b77dc6aca5470a356f\",\"quote\":\"(5) A generator shall mark or label the generator's container with the following:\\n\\n(a) The words \\\"Hazardous Waste\\\"; and\\n\\n(b) An indication of the hazards of the contents [examples include, but are not limited to, the applicable hazardous waste characteristics (i.e., ignitable, corrosive, reactive, toxic); hazard communication consistent with the department of transportation requirements at 49 CFR Part 172 subpart E (labeling) or subpart F (placarding); a hazard statement or pictogram consistent with the occupational safety and health administration hazard communication standard at 29 CFR 1910.1200; or a chemical hazard label consistent with the national fire protection association code 704].\",\"start\":3195},{\"end\":3895,\"field\":\"logic_text\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:3195:3895:sha256-dbc57e737acb25c82f0f782bff280c06f1e03967db4408b77dc6aca5470a356f\",\"quote\":\"(5) A generator shall mark or label the generator's container with the following:\\n\\n(a) The words \\\"Hazardous Waste\\\"; and\\n\\n(b) An indication of the hazards of the contents [examples include, but are not limited to, the applicable hazardous waste characteristics (i.e., ignitable, corrosive, reactive, toxic); hazard communication consistent with the department of transportation requirements at 49 CFR Part 172 subpart E (labeling) or subpart F (placarding); a hazard statement or pictogram consistent with the occupational safety and health administration hazard communication standard at 29 CFR 1910.1200; or a chemical hazard label consistent with the national fire protection association code 704].\",\"start\":3195},{\"end\":3216,\"field\":\"modality\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:3211:3216:sha256-56ee5b508706bf2de91712d85d6d1e11ddbff01949142ed6e8c22e3b1bed1c71\",\"quote\":\"shall\",\"start\":3211},{\"end\":3895,\"field\":\"choice_text\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:3195:3895:sha256-dbc57e737acb25c82f0f782bff280c06f1e03967db4408b77dc6aca5470a356f\",\"quote\":\"(5) A generator shall mark or label the generator's container with the following:\\n\\n(a) The words \\\"Hazardous Waste\\\"; and\\n\\n(b) An indication of the hazards of the contents [examples include, but are not limited to, the applicable hazardous waste characteristics (i.e., ignitable, corrosive, reactive, toxic); hazard communication consistent with the department of transportation requirements at 49 CFR Part 172 subpart E (labeling) or subpart F (placarding); a hazard statement or pictogram consistent with the occupational safety and health administration hazard communication standard at 29 CFR 1910.1200; or a chemical hazard label consistent with the national fire protection association code 704].\",\"start\":3195},{\"end\":1309,\"field\":\"scope_text:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:121:1309:sha256-b1f414f71874caa7cb1888a99a7de9b50bfee7c357001f3a76143b7503ec786d\",\"quote\":\"(A) A generator may accumulate as much as fifty-five gallons of non-acute hazardous waste and either one quart of liquid acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or one kilogram (kg) (2.2 pounds) of solid acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code in containers at or near any point of generation where wastes initially accumulate which is under the control of the operator of the process generating the waste, without a permit or permit by rule and without complying with the requirements of Chapters 3745-50, 3745-54 to 3745-57 and 3745-205, 3745-65 to 3745-69 and 3745-256, 3745-266, and 3745-267 of the Administrative Code, provided that all of the conditions for exemption in this rule are met. A generator may comply with the conditions for exemption in this rule instead of complying with the conditions for exemption in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code, except as required in paragraphs (A)(7) and (A)(8) of this rule. The conditions for exemption for satellite accumulation are:\",\"start\":121}],\"id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:ed06f99a8ed6c7a2f7c06914e85eebe6ba5486288278e137b3db22aa3f28e89b\",\"jurisdiction\":\"\",\"jurisdiction_quote\":\"\",\"kind\":\"requirement\",\"logic_text\":\"(5) A generator shall mark or label the generator's container with the following:\\n\\n(a) The words \\\"Hazardous Waste\\\"; and\\n\\n(b) An indication of the hazards of the contents [examples include, but are not limited to, the applicable hazardous waste characteristics (i.e., ignitable, corrosive, reactive, toxic); hazard communication consistent with the department of transportation requirements at 49 CFR Part 172 subpart E (labeling) or subpart F (placarding); a hazard statement or pictogram consistent with the occupational safety and health administration hazard communication standard at 29 CFR 1910.1200; or a chemical hazard label consistent with the national fire protection association code 704].\",\"meaning_assertion_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:8c8d3ea7c0a12d12de2905e3bac5b2c71b5a1ac103f0b8d07df7755b071e2f44\",\"modality\":\"must\",\"modality_quote\":\"shall\",\"object\":\"\",\"occurrence_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:occurrence:a26d5204bb4239b77188ddc0b4d0ba6b8845b24abca119a72a66d307a5282614\",\"origin\":\"aiSuggested\",\"quote\":\"(5) A generator shall mark or label the generator's container with the following:\\n\\n(a) The words \\\"Hazardous Waste\\\"; and\\n\\n(b) An indication of the hazards of the contents [examples include, but are not limited to, the applicable hazardous waste characteristics (i.e., ignitable, corrosive, reactive, toxic); hazard communication consistent with the department of transportation requirements at 49 CFR Part 172 subpart E (labeling) or subpart F (placarding); a hazard statement or pictogram consistent with the occupational safety and health administration hazard communication standard at 29 CFR 1910.1200; or a chemical hazard label consistent with the national fire protection association code 704].\",\"references\":[\"49 CFR Part 172 subpart E\",\"49 CFR Part 172 subpart F\",\"29 CFR 1910.1200\",\"national fire protection association code 704\"],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:f2af2006acb64bb0de933165a76f67e3d7adc0d483a35a262f494d2938305088\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(A) A generator may accumulate as much as fifty-five gallons of non-acute hazardous waste and either one quart of liquid acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or one kilogram (kg) (2.2 pounds) of solid acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code in containers at or near any point of generation where wastes initially accumulate which is under the control of the operator of the process generating the waste, without a permit or permit by rule and without complying with the requirements of Chapters 3745-50, 3745-54 to 3745-57 and 3745-205, 3745-65 to 3745-69 and 3745-256, 3745-266, and 3745-267 of the Administrative Code, provided that all of the conditions for exemption in this rule are met. A generator may comply with the conditions for exemption in this rule instead of complying with the conditions for exemption in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code, except as required in paragraphs (A)(7) and (A)(8) of this rule. The conditions for exemption for satellite accumulation are:\"],\"scope_text\":\"For satellite accumulation under the conditions for exemption in this rule.\",\"section_id\":\"section-1\",\"start\":3195,\"summary\":\"A generator shall mark or label the generator's container with both the words \\\"Hazardous Waste\\\" and an indication of the hazards of the contents [examples include, but are not limited to, the applicable hazardous waste characteristics (i.e., ignitable, corrosive, reactive, toxic); hazard communication consistent with the department of transportation requirements at 49 CFR Part 172 subpart E (labeling) or subpart F (placarding); a hazard statement or pictogram consistent with the occupational safety and health administration hazard communication standard at 29 CFR 1910.1200; or a chemical hazard label consistent with the national fire protection association code 704].\",\"target_ids\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
      "dcterms:references": [
        {
          "@id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:553d3e17b268e5326b809bb1f20317a77090a8a8f1d21c2507b7158de3751f8f"
