      "dcterms:description": "{\"action\":\"\",\"actor\":\"\",\"alternative_quotes\":[\"(a) Within three consecutive calendar days, comply with the applicable central accumulation area requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code; or\",\"(i) A central accumulation area operated in accordance with the applicable requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code;\",\"(ii) An on-site permit by rule or permitted treatment, storage, or disposal facility; or\",\"(iii) An off-site designated facility.\"],\"applies_to\":[],\"assertion_ids\":[\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:1170b1447579ba1f0ab047327b696eaf22b01d5077466105a6f4cd9ff420cea4\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:3b4a526d8ab691d1e6583898b39e90e134e53f3521dd9d601994368387844bc9\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:d2079158cead5073088a0eb8fec5bef88a80d4c1af62fb4f70c94f1927598d77\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:4f0d2c9f25f8233c32c8a62c55dc631f1d74b2d1103f6828f683446f039f243d\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:cb45843a39b12043cad06778551640ae2c488aaff1df6b7aa2b7f29ed76877ac\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:6feffbad55db270c6d3066258e0fece5a5bb7f0ffab822127fb6a237663fe820\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:563e204eb0af2c9e8d00bc2ff852b7a702eccd415f41ab988216a1506731f0cc\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:d3e6fb081aa80a3704d2febddd0e1c18a691b4a4cfa6e6ffcd3e90671e33e33a\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:fbd76f5ef83b21bb5e6ec723cbc8e3baf8bcdde814e87fc1844957b19cce3127\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:2f8e4039ee6527746b0cf6b933f6205bf62858d665e7b308eaead909643e54cf\"],\"choice_quote\":\"(6) A generator who accumulates either acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or non-acute hazardous waste in excess of the amounts listed in paragraph (A) of this rule at or near any point of generation shall do the following:\\n\\n(a) Within three consecutive calendar days, comply with the applicable central accumulation area requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code; or\\n\\n(b) Remove the excess from the satellite accumulation area within three consecutive calendar days to either:\\n\\n(i) A central accumulation area operated in accordance with the applicable requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code;\\n\\n(ii) An on-site permit by rule or permitted treatment, storage, or disposal facility; or\\n\\n(iii) An off-site designated facility.\",\"choice_text\":\"either (a) Within three consecutive calendar days, comply with the applicable central accumulation area requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code; or (b) Remove the excess from the satellite accumulation area within three consecutive calendar days to either: (i) A central accumulation area operated in accordance with the applicable requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code; (ii) An on-site permit by rule or permitted treatment, storage, or disposal facility; or (iii) An off-site designated facility.\",\"claimants\":[],\"concepts\":[],\"context_quotes\":[],\"effective_periods\":[],\"end\":4839,\"evidence\":[{\"end\":4839,\"field\":\"summary\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:3897:4839:sha256-ee4b38729ff23d70066e67b85080140e957ef7136661f406f8629abe120c9ad9\",\"quote\":\"(6) A generator who accumulates either acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or non-acute hazardous waste in excess of the amounts listed in paragraph (A) of this rule at or near any point of generation shall do the following:\\n\\n(a) Within three consecutive calendar days, comply with the applicable central accumulation area requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code; or\\n\\n(b) Remove the excess from the satellite accumulation area within three consecutive calendar days to either:\\n\\n(i) A central accumulation area operated in accordance with the applicable requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code;\\n\\n(ii) An on-site permit by rule or permitted treatment, storage, or disposal facility; or\\n\\n(iii) An off-site designated facility.\",\"start\":3897},{\"end\":4839,\"field\":\"logic_text\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:3897:4839:sha256-ee4b38729ff23d70066e67b85080140e957ef7136661f406f8629abe120c9ad9\",\"quote\":\"(6) A generator who accumulates either acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or non-acute hazardous waste in excess of the amounts listed in paragraph (A) of this rule at or near any point of generation shall do the following:\\n\\n(a) Within three consecutive calendar days, comply with the applicable central accumulation area requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code; or\\n\\n(b) Remove the excess from the satellite accumulation area within three consecutive calendar days to either:\\n\\n(i) A central accumulation area operated in accordance with the applicable requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code;\\n\\n(ii) An on-site permit by rule or permitted treatment, storage, or disposal facility; or\\n\\n(iii) An off-site designated facility.\",\"start\":3897},{\"end\":4178,\"field\":\"modality\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:4173:4178:sha256-56ee5b508706bf2de91712d85d6d1e11ddbff01949142ed6e8c22e3b1bed1c71\",\"quote\":\"shall\",\"start\":4173},{\"end\":4839,\"field\":\"choice_text\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:3897:4839:sha256-ee4b38729ff23d70066e67b85080140e957ef7136661f406f8629abe120c9ad9\",\"quote\":\"(6) A generator who accumulates either acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or non-acute hazardous waste in excess of the amounts listed in paragraph (A) of this rule at or near any point of generation shall do the following:\\n\\n(a) Within three consecutive calendar days, comply with the applicable central accumulation area requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code; or\\n\\n(b) Remove the excess from the satellite accumulation area within three consecutive calendar days to either:\\n\\n(i) A central accumulation area operated in accordance with the applicable requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code;\\n\\n(ii) An on-site permit by rule or permitted treatment, storage, or disposal facility; or\\n\\n(iii) An off-site designated facility.\",\"start\":3897},{\"end\":1309,\"field\":\"scope_text:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:121:1309:sha256-b1f414f71874caa7cb1888a99a7de9b50bfee7c357001f3a76143b7503ec786d\",\"quote\":\"(A) A generator may accumulate as much as fifty-five gallons of non-acute hazardous waste and either one quart of liquid acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or one kilogram (kg) (2.2 pounds) of solid acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code in containers at or near any point of generation where wastes initially accumulate which is under the control of the operator of the process generating the waste, without a permit or permit by rule and without complying with the requirements of Chapters 3745-50, 3745-54 to 3745-57 and 3745-205, 3745-65 to 3745-69 and 3745-256, 3745-266, and 3745-267 of the Administrative Code, provided that all of the conditions for exemption in this rule are met. A generator may comply with the conditions for exemption in this rule instead of complying with the conditions for exemption in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code, except as required in paragraphs (A)(7) and (A)(8) of this rule. The conditions for exemption for satellite accumulation are:\",\"start\":121},{\"end\":4196,\"field\":\"scope_text:1\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:3897:4196:sha256-e12a5693cb831954a45bb8682b13d13bfb64ae96a34daa54d95a02887c4019fe\",\"quote\":\"(6) A generator who accumulates either acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or non-acute hazardous waste in excess of the amounts listed in paragraph (A) of this rule at or near any point of generation shall do the following:\",\"start\":3897},{\"end\":4410,\"field\":\"alternative:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:4198:4410:sha256-a7f31af7c795e76560a098d666b412b3cfa555cbc12486402a47af9436e9d88c\",\"quote\":\"(a) Within three consecutive calendar days, comply with the applicable central accumulation area requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code; or\",\"start\":4198},{\"end\":4709,\"field\":\"alternative:1\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:4522:4709:sha256-d1c8b94f1568f0d78ee8d917461f71a9e65f20c88cc03c565e5c686a8abef9e0\",\"quote\":\"(i) A central accumulation area operated in accordance with the applicable requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code;\",\"start\":4522},{\"end\":4799,\"field\":\"alternative:2\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:4711:4799:sha256-cfadd40d9097d6e790a06d84b15fd90258777975345953faf97bac50738d4963\",\"quote\":\"(ii) An on-site permit by rule or permitted treatment, storage, or disposal facility; or\",\"start\":4711},{\"end\":4839,\"field\":\"alternative:3\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A43f75aaf4a19870db19d481dd6883f99ef4c606c7cb4914012a118a12fbce149:4801:4839:sha256-bc1a0639bde3524d54e011b611b7cf02f957f6cda512ff7eff2f6c40727f08cd\",\"quote\":\"(iii) An off-site designated facility.\",\"start\":4801}],\"id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:4c8a69af1b926c8cc6a50c38ced9457fc38dfc3cb55487590aa71cf256b18bb4\",\"jurisdiction\":\"\",\"jurisdiction_quote\":\"\",\"kind\":\"requirement\",\"logic_text\":\"(6) A generator who accumulates either acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or non-acute hazardous waste in excess of the amounts listed in paragraph (A) of this rule at or near any point of generation shall do the following:\\n\\n(a) Within three consecutive calendar days, comply with the applicable central accumulation area requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code; or\\n\\n(b) Remove the excess from the satellite accumulation area within three consecutive calendar days to either:\\n\\n(i) A central accumulation area operated in accordance with the applicable requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code;\\n\\n(ii) An on-site permit by rule or permitted treatment, storage, or disposal facility; or\\n\\n(iii) An off-site designated facility.\",\"meaning_assertion_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:2f8e4039ee6527746b0cf6b933f6205bf62858d665e7b308eaead909643e54cf\",\"modality\":\"must\",\"modality_quote\":\"shall\",\"object\":\"\",\"occurrence_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:occurrence:a0d934d875e0557ccd31802500da14535b81480fc63d9e1147ae59d5fe65ab0b\",\"origin\":\"aiSuggested\",\"quote\":\"(6) A generator who accumulates either acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or non-acute hazardous waste in excess of the amounts listed in paragraph (A) of this rule at or near any point of generation shall do the following:\\n\\n(a) Within three consecutive calendar days, comply with the applicable central accumulation area requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code; or\\n\\n(b) Remove the excess from the satellite accumulation area within three consecutive calendar days to either:\\n\\n(i) A central accumulation area operated in accordance with the applicable requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code;\\n\\n(ii) An on-site permit by rule or permitted treatment, storage, or disposal facility; or\\n\\n(iii) An off-site designated facility.\",\"references\":[\"rule 3745-51-31\",\"paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33\",\"paragraph (A) of this rule\",\"paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16\",\"paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17\"],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:5994ed69991b50d93dac432dc4256e48d30ed62de7bd37af0065899ade4cd42a\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(A) A generator may accumulate as much as fifty-five gallons of non-acute hazardous waste and either one quart of liquid acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or one kilogram (kg) (2.2 pounds) of solid acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code in containers at or near any point of generation where wastes initially accumulate which is under the control of the operator of the process generating the waste, without a permit or permit by rule and without complying with the requirements of Chapters 3745-50, 3745-54 to 3745-57 and 3745-205, 3745-65 to 3745-69 and 3745-256, 3745-266, and 3745-267 of the Administrative Code, provided that all of the conditions for exemption in this rule are met. A generator may comply with the conditions for exemption in this rule instead of complying with the conditions for exemption in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code, except as required in paragraphs (A)(7) and (A)(8) of this rule. The conditions for exemption for satellite accumulation are:\",\"(6) A generator who accumulates either acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or non-acute hazardous waste in excess of the amounts listed in paragraph (A) of this rule at or near any point of generation shall do the following:\"],\"scope_text\":\"When a generator accumulates either acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or non-acute hazardous waste in excess of the amounts listed in paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-15 at or near any point of generation.\",\"section_id\":\"section-1\",\"start\":3897,\"summary\":\"A generator who accumulates either acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or non-acute hazardous waste in excess of the amounts listed in paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-15 at or near any point of generation shall, within three consecutive calendar days, comply with the applicable central accumulation area requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code, or remove the excess from the satellite accumulation area within three consecutive calendar days to either a central accumulation area operated in accordance with the applicable requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code, an on-site permit by rule or permitted treatment, storage, or disposal facility, or an off-site designated facility.\",\"target_ids\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
